WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.250
Let's make Pictures in the snow.

2
00:00:02.630 --> 00:00:07.476
Make a flat snow picture by drawing an outline, adding low shapes and pressing

3
00:00:07.476 --> 00:00:08.860
patterns into the surface.

4
00:00:09.240 --> 00:00:11.320
Make this project with a grown-up.

5
00:00:11.700 --> 00:00:14.430
Gather the supplies listed below the video.

6
00:00:14.810 --> 00:00:17.055
Pause whenever you need more time.

7
00:00:17.435 --> 00:00:20.545
An adult checks the location and weather and stays close.

8
00:00:20.925 --> 00:00:25.690
Keep the picture flat and low, with no digging, tunnels or tall structures.

9
00:00:27.167 --> 00:00:28.357
Step 1.

10
00:00:28.737 --> 00:00:30.312
Smooth a snow canvas.

11
00:00:30.692 --> 00:00:33.732
Choose a flat patch about 40 centimetres wide.

12
00:00:34.112 --> 00:00:37.617
Pat the surface with mittened hands until it is gently even.

13
00:00:37.997 --> 00:00:40.997
Leave the snow on the ground rather than digging a hole.

14
00:00:41.377 --> 00:00:42.757
Grown-up help.

15
00:00:43.137 --> 00:00:45.582
Choose a safe area and check clothing.

16
00:00:47.000 --> 00:00:48.180
Step 2.

17
00:00:48.560 --> 00:00:50.285
Draw a broad outline.

18
00:00:50.665 --> 00:00:54.780
Use the blunt twig to draw a large circle, flower or animal head.

19
00:00:55.160 --> 00:00:58.800
Keep the outline simple enough to follow with one finger.

20
00:00:59.180 --> 00:01:00.560
Grown-up help.

21
00:01:00.940 --> 00:01:02.945
Guide the outline if needed.

22
00:01:04.334 --> 00:01:05.679
Step 3.

23
00:01:06.059 --> 00:01:07.644
Add low raised shapes.

24
00:01:08.024 --> 00:01:11.214
Place small handfuls of snow inside the outline.

25
00:01:11.594 --> 00:01:15.574
Press them into shallow mounds no more than about 3 centimetres high.

26
00:01:15.954 --> 00:01:18.984
Add round cheeks, petals or two broad ears.

27
00:01:19.364 --> 00:01:20.744
Grown-up help.

28
00:01:21.124 --> 00:01:23.574
Help pack pieces that crumble.

29
00:01:25.001 --> 00:01:26.151
Step 4.

30
00:01:26.531 --> 00:01:28.051
Press a pattern.

31
00:01:28.431 --> 00:01:32.341
Use the twig tip or a mitten edge to press shallow dots and lines.

32
00:01:32.721 --> 00:01:37.191
Add eyes and a smile, petal lines or a fur pattern without making deep

33
00:01:37.191 --> 00:01:37.511
holes.

34
00:01:37.891 --> 00:01:39.271
Grown-up help.

35
00:01:39.651 --> 00:01:41.546
Supervise the blunt tool.

36
00:01:43.001 --> 00:01:44.176
Step 5.

37
00:01:44.556 --> 00:01:46.441
Give the picture a name.

38
00:01:46.821 --> 00:01:50.616
Stand beside the picture and look down at the shapes and shadows.

39
00:01:50.996 --> 00:01:54.081
Name it, collect the twig and take a warm-up break.

40
00:01:54.461 --> 00:01:56.466
Leave only snow behind.

41
00:01:56.846 --> 00:01:58.226
Grown-up help.

42
00:01:58.606 --> 00:02:00.916
Check comfort and gather the tool.

43
00:02:02.334 --> 00:02:05.249
Here are three ideas for your finished project.

44
00:02:05.629 --> 00:02:09.179
These example pictures were made with artificial intelligence.

45
00:02:09.559 --> 00:02:11.579
Your creation can look different.

46
00:02:11.959 --> 00:02:14.129
Take the twig and all equipment home.

47
00:02:14.509 --> 00:02:19.656
The picture changes with light, weather and melting; save a photo or drawing if

48
00:02:19.656 --> 00:02:20.024
desired.

49
00:02:20.404 --> 00:02:21.394
Well done.

50
00:02:21.774 --> 00:02:24.204
Take a moment to enjoy what you made.

